<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    RM_TheSump                                      THESUMP_RM_MOD_BUILD_1 - Phase A
    Phase A row 23 of design/RimMandrake/biome_mod_architecture.md. Parent:
    BIOME_MOD_SPLIT_EXECUTION_1. Governed by BIOME_PAINT_ONCE_AT_THE_END_1 - this
    def is expected to carry 0 tiles until the terminal repaint; that is not a
    defect.

    Copied from the frozen src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Defs/BiomeDefs/RUT_Sump.xml
    (kept, unchanged except a header comment, still carrying the live campaign
    world's painted tiles). This is a NEW, franchise-free sibling for any other
    generated RimWorld planet, not a rename of that one.

    RM tier: nothing here knows what campaign or planet uses it. NOT donor-free:
    terrain (AB_GrassySand/AB_LushGrass), the world-map texture (Biomes/AB_TarPits)
    and one wildPlants row (AB_TarPuddle) are all Alpha Biomes' own, unchanged from
    the twin — same honesty standard every sibling RM_ biome mod ships (compare
    RM_Miasma's own header).

    workerClass: replaces the donor AlphaBiomes.BiomeWorker_TarPits with this
    mod's own RM_BiomeWorker_TheSump (RM_TheSumpBiome.cs) - a donor type in
    workerClass is a hard dependency the RimMandrake tier may not assume
    (biome_mod_architecture.md Sec5 step 2).

    wildAnimals: 4 rows ship inline, all Alpha Animals donor rows individually
    MayRequire-gated (unchanged from the twin's 3, plus AA_BumbledroneQueen added
    per rosters/the_sump.json's own "goes with the rest of the bumbledrones" ruling
    - THESUMP_RM_MOD_BUILD_1 §5/§3). RSW_Hssiss (the biome's one seated canon beast,
    ruled 2026-09-10) does NOT ship here - it rides Utinni's WildAnimals_Sump.xml as
    a PatchOperationAdd onto this def instead, MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary",
    per the Q11a naming-tier ruling (SUMP_UTINNI_LAYER_1 §3).

    SUMP_FAUNA_ROSTER_1 (2026-09-25/26): five invented rows added -
    RM_SumpMouse (0.8), RM_Brommet (0.4), RM_Dredgel (0.2), RM_Skarrid (0.25),
    RM_Skellarn (0.15) - per sump_fauna_roster_2026-09-24.md. These five have
    no existing donor slot to evict: the mouse's placeholder was never wired
    into wildAnimals at all, and the other four are wholly new niches. The
    OTHER four rows the roster names (RM_Gulveth, RM_Thrummel,
    RM_ThrummelWarden, RM_ThrummelBroodmother) are built in full
    (ThingDefs_Races/RM_SumpFauna.xml) but deliberately NOT wired here - the
    doc's own §7 marks replacing today's AA_TarGuzzler/AA_Bumbledrone/
    AA_BumbledroneHierophant/AA_BumbledroneQueen rows "PROPOSED for this
    biome's own sitting, executed by nobody here", per the owner's standing
    evictions-are-stopped ruling (2026-09-22). The 4 donor rows below are
    UNCHANGED this pass.

    wildPlants: AB_TarPuddle carries a fresh MayRequire="sarg.alphabiomes" here
    that the twin's own copy never needed (same-mod, no gate required there) -
    same posture RM_Miasma's own wildPlants notes already establish for a donor
    row moved into a standalone mod.

    terrainsByFertility: both rows gain the same MayRequire="sarg.alphabiomes"
    guard for the same reason.

    biomeMapConditions: RUT_SumpDuskLock baked in directly (not via a second patch
    op) - it now lives in this SAME mod (Patches/RUT_SumpDuskLock_BiomeWiring.xml
    wires it onto RUT_Sump alone; this def references it natively), matching the
    precedent RM_Miasma.xml actually shipped for RUT_MiasmaWeatherLock.

    modExtensions: unchanged in shape from the twin - BiomeGlowMultiplierExtension
    and RM_CarriedFilthHediffExtension both already live in the shared
    mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards and reference RUT_Tarred/RM_Filth_Tar, which
    stay exactly where they are (UtinniPatches / shared EnvironmentalHazards
    respectively) - nothing here needed retargeting.

    texture (Biomes/AB_TarPits) is inherited unchanged from the twin, same
    posture as every sibling's donor world-map texture - not this build's scope
    to fix.

    SUMP_FLORA_ROSTER_1 (2026-09-25): plantDensity corrected 0.15 -> 0.25 and
    forageability corrected 0.0 -> 0.8. Both values contradicted the frozen
    sheet's own ruling (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/the_sump.md SS0:
    "forageability 0.8 re-pointed at the edge-flora... plantDensity 0.25 fits
    the edge-ring pattern") AND the RUT_Sump twin's OWN header comment two
    lines above its fields, which already states the correct numbers; the
    twin's fields themselves were wrong at authoring time and this copy
    inherited the error verbatim. The frozen RUT_Sump.xml twin is NOT touched
    (carries the live campaign world; do not edit); this fix lands only on
    this def, which still carries 0 tiles pending the terminal repaint.
    forageability 0.8 now has a real referent: RM_Skelver (RM_SumpFlora.xml,
    this same pass) is "the row that SS0's forageability 0.8 actually points
    at" per sump_flora_roster_2026-09-24.md SS3 row 3.
  -->

  <BiomeDef>
    <defName>RM_TheSump</defName>
    <label>the Sump</label>
    <description>The planet's oil sump: the lowest basin on Ash'karr, filled by every slow black flow off the twilight slopes for geological time. Flat black pools and cooled glassy sheets under permanent dusk, ringed with low waxy plants that glow faintly where the Junker stations keep their lamp-gardens. Mice run the tar without a thought. Nothing else touches it -- because the tar takes slowly, keeps perfectly, and everything that ever blundered in is still in there.</description>
    <workerClass>RimMandrake.TheSump.RM_BiomeWorker_TheSump</workerClass>

    <allowRoads>true</allowRoads>
    <allowRivers>true</allowRivers>
    <allowFarmingCamps>true</allowFarmingCamps>
    <animalDensity>1.0</animalDensity>
    <plantDensity>0.25</plantDensity>
    <forageability>0.8</forageability>
    <movementDifficulty>4</movementDifficulty>
    <texture>Biomes/AB_TarPits</texture>
    <diseaseMtbDays>65</diseaseMtbDays>
    <diseases>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Flu</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_Plague</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>100</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_GutWorms</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>60</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_MuscleParasites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>60</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_FibrousMechanites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>30</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <diseaseInc>Disease_SensoryMechanites</diseaseInc>
        <commonality>30</commonality>
      </li>
    </diseases>
    <terrainsByFertility>
      <li MayRequire="sarg.alphabiomes">
        <terrain>AB_GrassySand</terrain>
        <min>-999</min>
        <max>0.25</max>
      </li>
      <li MayRequire="sarg.alphabiomes">
        <terrain>AB_LushGrass</terrain>
        <min>0.25</min>
        <max>999</max>
      </li>
    </terrainsByFertility>
    <baseWeatherCommonalities>
      <Fog>50</Fog>
      <Clear>15</Clear>
      <DryThunderstorm>1</DryThunderstorm>
      <Rain>0</Rain>
      <RainyThunderstorm>0</RainyThunderstorm>
      <FoggyRain>0</FoggyRain>
      <SnowGentle>2</SnowGentle>
      <SnowHard>2</SnowHard>
    </baseWeatherCommonalities>
    <biomeMapConditions>
      <li MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">RUT_SumpDuskLock</li>
    </biomeMapConditions>
    <wildAnimals>
      <AA_TarGuzzler MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.5</AA_TarGuzzler>  <!-- tar guzzler - tar-eater, adjust-keep -->
      <AA_Bumbledrone MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.35</AA_Bumbledrone>  <!-- bumbledrone - under-layer, keep -->
      <AA_BumbledroneHierophant MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.2</AA_BumbledroneHierophant>  <!-- bumbledrone hierophant - under-layer, keep -->
      <AA_BumbledroneQueen MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">0.5</AA_BumbledroneQueen>  <!-- bumbledrone queen - rides the hive verdict, roster round-2 move mapping -->
      <!-- SUMP_FAUNA_ROSTER_1: 5 wholly-new rows, no donor slot evicted (see
           header). RM_Gulveth/RM_Thrummel/RM_ThrummelWarden/
           RM_ThrummelBroodmother are built but not wired - PROPOSED
           donor-replacement dispositions await the Sump's own sitting. -->
      <RM_SumpMouse>0.8</RM_SumpMouse>  <!-- sump-mouse - the instrument, the prey base -->
      <RM_Brommet>0.4</RM_Brommet>  <!-- brommet - the ring's ordinary grazer -->
      <RM_Dredgel>0.2</RM_Dredgel>  <!-- dredgel - the archive's janitor -->
      <RM_Skarrid>0.25</RM_Skarrid>  <!-- skarrid - the still hunter -->
      <RM_Skellarn>0.15</RM_Skellarn>  <!-- skellarn - the stilt-flier, ruled 2026-09-24 -->
    </wildAnimals>
    <coastalWildAnimals />
    <wildPlants>
      <!-- SUMP_FLORA_ROSTER_1 (2026-09-25): AB_TarPuddle replaced 1:1 by our
           own RM_Velloch, same job same commonality (roster doc SS5). The
           other 8 rows are new; RUT_Plant_Wick (already shipped, this mod)
           gains its first wild-presence row here per the roster doc's own
           "wild [wick/dorvel] at low commonality... starter stock" language.
           Commonalities: INVENTED-BUILD except RM_Dorvel (0.05) and
           RM_Velloch (0.6), both named exactly in the doc; see
           RM_SumpFlora.xml's header for the full rationale. -->
      <RUT_Plant_Wick>0.03</RUT_Plant_Wick>  <!-- wick-plant - starter stock -->
      <RM_Dorvel>0.05</RM_Dorvel>  <!-- dorvel - starter stock, doc-named -->
      <RM_Skelver>0.4</RM_Skelver>  <!-- skelver - forage staple, baseline green -->
      <RM_Korveth>0.15</RM_Korveth>  <!-- korveth - bitumen accumulator -->
      <RM_Brindeth>0.2</RM_Brindeth>  <!-- brindeth - outer-ring woody margin -->
      <RM_Soffeth>0.08</RM_Soffeth>  <!-- soffeth - seep-mouth breather's tell -->
      <RM_Tolleth>0.03</RM_Tolleth>  <!-- tolleth - rare grave-bloom marker -->
      <RM_Velloch MayRequire="mandrake.rm.flowworks">0.6</RM_Velloch>  <!-- velloch - tar-surface film, replaces AB_TarPuddle -->
      <RM_Mirrelin>0.35</RM_Mirrelin>  <!-- mirrelin - glass-reach graze -->
      <RM_Pallick>0.05</RM_Pallick>  <!-- pallick - rare false-floor lie -->
    </wildPlants>
    <wildPlantRegrowDays>20</wildPlantRegrowDays>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.BiomeGlowMultiplierExtension" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
        <glowMultiplier>0.55</glowMultiplier>
        <suppressSunlightStatAffecter>true</suppressSunlightStatAffecter>
      </li>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_CarriedFilthHediffExtension" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
        <filthDef>RM_Filth_Tar</filthDef>
        <hediffDef>RUT_Tarred</hediffDef>
      </li>
      <!-- BIOME_ARRIVAL_NARRATION_1: RM tier, plain reads, no character. The
           Utinni layer (src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Patches/
           BiomeArrivalLetters_TheSump.xml) replaces both fields below with
           the campaign Narrator's own voice via PatchOperationReplace. -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_BiomeArrivalLetterExtension" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
        <letterLabel>The Sump</letterLabel>
        <letterText>The tar keeps whatever slips into it, so read the surface before you cross it. Watch the mice: where their lines bend, the crust underneath has gone thin. An unbroken pale crust that no line ever touches is not solid ground, it is a lie. And wherever soffeth grows in a ring, there is gas rising through the tar below.</letterText>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </BiomeDef>

</Defs>
